How many widget-test bodies check nothing but
`expect(tester.takeException(), isNull)`, less the ones excused with a
reason in `scripts/check_thin_assertions.py`.

A CEILING, and it may only fall. It was 34 when the hunt started -- all
of them in `dialogs_build_batch2_test.dart` -- and twenty-nine have been
rewritten, which turned up four wrong-shape fixtures and two real
defects. The remaining five are named in docs/handoff.md.

It went 14 -> 11 -> 7 -> 6 -> 5 and EVERY step was the gate refusing the
stale number, not somebody remembering to lower it. That under-ceiling arm is
the half of a ratchet nobody writes and the half that keeps the ground
won.

Thirteen more bodies match the pattern and are excused in `ALLOWED`:
twelve are overflow tests, where the framework raising on `RenderFlex` IS
the assertion and `takeException` is what collects it, and one writes a
spreadsheet that `check_xlsx.py` reads back in the same job.
